            "review_title": "Review at Poke Fresh",
            "review_text": "ngoctrantran\nSan Jose, California315 contributions\n0\nNot bad, but definitely not enough.\nJan 2019\nPoke is diced raw fish. Here, there are only few types to choose from: tuna, spicy tuna or salmon 😑. Nothing fancy for the choices of toppings either. My basic bowl, consists of two types of raw fish, tobiko, crab salad (totally misleading since it just imitation crab, with no dressing or ‘salad’), avocado, seaweed salad, is above 200,000vnd. It’s not cheap for Vietnamese Poke standard. What disappoints me the most is the room temperature inside the restaurant. I prefer to dine with good air conditioning room, especially if I’m eating raw fish. Poke Fresh dining room is not cool enough for me to linger around.\nRead more\nWritten January 28, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
